# cmd.exe is the reason this file exists. A .bat checked out with bare LF endings can make
# `goto` jump to the wrong place, which is exactly the kind of failure that shows up as a
# window closing without a message. Force CRLF on checkout, and keep the shell script LF so
# it stays runnable if someone clones on Windows and copies it to a server.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.sh  text eol=lf
